# The same two figures, both made in the body of `compare`: two `plt.subplots()` calls, each a figure of its own (#175).
# No value beyond a call holds what it makes (`fig` and `other` are dropped, `ax` and `bx` drawn on by the body itself), so
# each figure is its call's: one step that makes two, each named by that step.

route notebooks.compare
step compare/compare
step compare/compare/subplots                                       # `fig, ax = plt.subplots()`
step compare/compare/subplots#2                                     # `other, bx = plt.subplots()`

line entry > compare call
line compare/compare/subplots > _·fig@compare/compare/subplots value
line compare/compare/subplots > _·ax@compare/compare/subplots value
line compare/compare/subplots#2 > _·other@compare/compare/subplots#2 value
line compare/compare/subplots#2 > _·bx@compare/compare/subplots#2 value
line _·ax@compare/compare/subplots > compare/compare value                             # `ax.set_title(..)`, `ax.plot(..)`
line _·bx@compare/compare/subplots#2 > compare/compare value
line compare/compare > Figure 1 · compare own
line compare/compare > Figure 2 · compare own                       # a second figure, by a second call

home _·fig@compare/compare/subplots compare/compare
home _·ax@compare/compare/subplots compare/compare
home _·other@compare/compare/subplots#2 compare/compare
home _·bx@compare/compare/subplots#2 compare/compare

side entry left
side Figure 1 · compare right
side Figure 2 · compare right
